NAME: Monday scoreboard
OWNER: Forecast
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Mondays at 6:03 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Monday scoreboard" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/forecast/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-forecast.md yet, record it (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH; yes: note it and tell TMEC Command to carry it out; no: mark it declined; change: refile once as a new item) and add its id and the outcome to the sent keys so it is never read twice. TMEC Command may already have nudged you in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-forecast/ and do it first (Tommy's Claude Code ads figures arrive here; note them as "reported by Tommy's Claude Code", read only).
Then use the scoreboard skill to write /workspace/tmec-team/data/forecast/scoreboard-<today>.md for the week Saturday to Friday just ended: every lead source against the bought-lead line, UNKNOWN where a source has no data. This report always goes out, so never write NO_CHANGE.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/forecast.md (if the Rebate watch routine already wrote it today, which happens when the 1st is a Monday, append a section and never overwrite it): the summary (at most 8 lines: best and worst source against the line, anything UNKNOWN and why, anything LOW sample, days to the next rebate step if inside 30), and anything blocked. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
